. A mean, of course, is taken as before. On my asking Mr. Stone (now Astronomer at Oxford, then chief assistant at Greenwich Observatory) as to the relative degree of accuracy of the two methods, he told me that he considered the first gave results to one-tenth, and the second to one-twentieth of a second.
